/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate33_vp_nHexylAcetate -- the vapour pressure of nHexylAcetate, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 steps 2 and 3).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate
  vp nHexylAcetate`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je050141m                14 pts  397.97-439.98 K  Schmitt; Hasse
      10.1016/j.jct.2005.08.003        13 pts  274.5-309.1 K  Krasnykh; Verevkin; Koutek; Doubsky
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      (none)

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/je050141m (14 pts, 397.97-439.98 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1016/j.jct.2005.08.003 (13 pts,
  274.5-309.1 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 7.2 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 13 points (7.08 to 7.24 %, mean 7.125 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 444.65 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 274.5-439.98 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  OBJECTIVE (C281 step 3, declared): `objective { method twoStage; }` --
  Vitor's fitting practice (DEV.md 4c C280): least squares in log10 P for a
  first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in P, (P_model - P)/P, over
  the fit points minimised from it; both answers are kept in the result.  A
  student who prefers another objective declares `leastSquares` or `minimax`.

  EARLIER FIT, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.198146 - 1539.5515/(T + -77.2388),
  in-sample R2 0.999994 over 14 points, 397.97-439.98 K. HELD OUT: 13
  points, AAD 5.8948 % against the band 7.2 % -> validated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 444.46 K. PROMOTED (and since
  REVERTED by `choupo-curate revert`) on 2026-11-10 into
  data/standards/components/nHexylAcetate.dat as reviewStatus
  autoPromoted, humanReviewed false, because: verdict validated, normal
  boiling point 444.46 K within 2 K of the record's Tb 444.65 K
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.228762 - 1562.4512/(T +
  -74.4887), in-sample R2 0.999992 over 14 points, 397.97-439.98 K. HELD
  OUT: 13 points, AAD 9.3708 % (max 14.0038 %) against the band 7.2 % ->
  notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares answer on the same points: AAD
  5.8948 %, max 10.2435 %. Its own normal boiling point (101.325 kPa):
  444.47 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict notValidated (AAD 9.371 %
  against the band 7.2 % declared before the fit); the record keeps
  AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  nHexylAcetate;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/nHexylAcetate-vapourPressure-je050141m.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je050141m"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/nHexylAcetate-vapourPressure-j.jct.2005.08.003.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.jct.2005.08.003"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  7.2 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 13 points (7.08 to 7.24 %, mean 7.125 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        objective  { method twoStage; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
